 "footnotes": [
  {
   "id": "c-fig-9-3",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The book cites Figure 9.3. The Λ system it describes is drawn in Figure 5.2."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-eq-5-20",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The book prints the number (5.20) on an empty line under (5.19); no equation is missing."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-schrodinger",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The book prints $i\\hbar|\\kpsi\\rangle = \\kHeff|\\kpsi\\rangle$ without the time derivative. The Schrodinger equation is $i\\hbar\\frac{d}{d\\kt}|\\kpsi\\rangle = \\kHeff|\\kpsi\\rangle$."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-real-complex",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The book writes “real and complex parts”. The second is the imaginary part of the denominator, $-i\\kdeltaprime$."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-fig-7-3",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The book cites Figure 7.3. The three-level configurations are drawn in Figure 5.1, at the opening of this chapter."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-eq-5-21",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "Eq. (5.21) adds the decay terms with $\\hbar$ to the Hamiltonian of Eq. (5.1), which carries none. In the frequency units of Eq. (5.1) the decay terms are $-\\frac{i\\kgammathree}{2}|3\\rangle\\langle 3| - \\frac{i\\kgammatwo}{2}|2\\rangle\\langle 2|$, as the equations of motion that follow use them."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-eq-5-10",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The book prints $+i[\\kH, \\rho]$, with only $\\mathcal{L}_{31}$ and $\\mathcal{L}_{32}$. The equations of motion (5.12)–(5.16) that follow are those of $\\dot{\\rho} = \\mathcal{L}_{31}(\\rho) + \\mathcal{L}_{32}(\\rho) + \\mathcal{L}_{21}(\\rho) - i[\\kH, \\rho]$: the Schrodinger evolution $-i[\\kH, \\rho]$ for $\\kH$ in units of $\\hbar$, with the decay at $\\gamma'$ from $|2\\rangle$ to $|1\\rangle$ included."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-eq-5-38",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "With the Hamiltonian (5.1), whose couplings carry a minus sign, the states to first order in $\\kOmegatwo/\\kDelta$ are $|+\\rangle \\approx |3\\rangle + \\frac{\\kOmegatwo^*}{\\kDelta}|2\\rangle$ and $|-\\rangle \\approx |2\\rangle - \\frac{\\kOmegatwo}{\\kDelta}|3\\rangle$; the admixture of $|3\\rangle$ in $|-\\rangle$ is the $-\\kOmegatwo/\\kDelta$ that (5.6) gives $\\kcthree$ when $\\kctwo = 1$. The book prints both with the opposite sign. The widths that follow depend only on $|\\kOmegatwo|^2/\\kDelta^2$ and are unchanged."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-eq-5-31",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The book leaves out the density of atoms. The susceptibility is the polarization of $N/\\kV$ atoms per unit field, as in Eq. (4.43): $\\kchione = \\frac{N}{\\kV}\\frac{|\\kmu|^2}{\\hbar\\epsilon_0}\\frac{\\krhothreeone}{\\kOmegaone}$."
  }
 ],
